<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Free State of Anhalt</h1><p class="st-meta">1918 CE – 1945 CE · capital Dessau</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Small central German republic that hosted the Bauhaus at Dessau and in 1932 became the first state with a Nazi head of government.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joachim-ernst-duke-of-anhalt">Joachim Ernst</a>'s regent abdicated in November 1918, and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-anhalt">Duchy of Anhalt</a> became a free state, with a democratic constitution adopted in 1919 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dessau">Dessau</a> as capital.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-anhalt">Anhalt</a> was governed by Social Democratic coalitions for most of the 1920s. Its industries included the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/junkers">Junkers</a> aircraft works and chemical plants at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bitterfeld">Bitterfeld</a> nearby. In 1925 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bauhaus">Bauhaus</a> moved from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weimar">Weimar</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dessau">Dessau</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/walter-gropius">Walter Gropius</a> designed its new building. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nazi-party">Nazis</a> won the 1932 state election, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfred-freyberg">Alfred Freyberg</a> became the first Nazi minister-president of a German state, and the Bauhaus was forced out that year.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nazi-party">Nazis</a> subordinated <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-anhalt">Anhalt</a> to a Reich governor. In 1945 it was occupied and placed in the Soviet zone, where it was merged with the Prussian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/province-of-saxony">Province of Saxony</a> to form the province, later Land, of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony-anhalt">Saxony-Anhalt</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/free-state-of-anhalt.jpg" alt="Free State of Anhalt" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: David Liuzzo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flagge_Herzogtum_Anhalt.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1918 CE – 1945 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Dessau</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Alfred Freyberg</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Freistaat Anhalt</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1932&amp;focus=free-state-of-anhalt" aria-label="Free State of Anhalt on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4956 385 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Free State of Anhalt lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5276 641L5276 641M5276 641L5300 622M5276 641L5300 622"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5276 641h0M5300 622h0M5300 622h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5276 641h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5276 641h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Dessau. <a href="/atlas?year=1932&amp;focus=free-state-of-anhalt">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
